  * toupper/tolower are the C-library ones in the "C" locale. The binary never
    calls setlocale (no setlocale symbol; identical output under LC_ALL=C /
    en_US.UTF-8 / tr_TR.UTF-8 / de_DE.ISO-8859-1). So the mapping is
    ASCII-only: 'a'..'z' <-> 'A'..'Z'; every other byte (0x00..0x40, 0x5B..0x60,
    0x7B..0xFF) is left unchanged.
  * The acronyms table is NOT consulted ("HTML" -> "Html").
  * No trimming, no word splitting, no separator handling: byte 0 upcased,
    every other byte downcased.
  * Empty string -> empty string.

